    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0638" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115P51/50</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-04T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2029. Your 1473 and my 1998 of April 27 regarding the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Joseph W. Fordney</hi>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d552-f1"/> Have requested
                    Legation at Stockholm to investigate matter of consignee of cargo at Malmö.
                    Understand firm of E. Klingener exists at Goteborg but does not appear as
                    existing at Malmo. Should he have branch house at Malmo will immediately present
                    facts to British Government and request release of vessel and cargo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
